  "description": "BILWIE crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H100 Cl8 Er4 Mn8 N8 O54,4(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn6 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn7 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn8 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 15 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.799-3.852 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 90.59-130.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H126Cl8Tb4Mn8N8O63. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Tb(III).",
